an explosion at a chemical plant in  Texas rocked an entire neighborhood  overnight prompting evacuations there  that stretched over half a mile radius  doorbell video shows a moment of the  explosion in Port Neches witnesses say  it was felt miles away police say there  is extensive damage throughout the city  the company that owns this plant says  three people have minor injuries now the  fire is still burning in Port Neches  which is about 85 miles east of Houston  Michele joy of our Houston affiliate  that's KHOU reports from near the scene  good morning the plant where this  explosion happened produces chemical and  petroleum based products however the  exact cause remains under investigation  video posted to social media shows just  how intense these flames were people  living in Port Neches say they heard a  blast shortly after 1:00 a.m. the  explosion blew out windows of homes that  were several miles away emergency  response crews went door-to-door  evacuating people from their homes as  the fire burned out of control there are  also reports of damage to area  businesses and a school this part of  Texas is a major hub for oil and gas  industries the company that owns the  plant says on its website that it  employs more than 200 people for CBS  this morning I'm Michele Choi
 

